            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0408" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.20 Mission/11a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-21T22:00:00-04:00">April 21, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>243. The agreement signed on November 27, 1943 providing for the assignment of a
                    United States Military Mission to Iran (Schwarzkopf) expires on October 2,
                    1944.</p>
                <p>Please ascertain discreetly and inform the Department by cable whether the
                    Iranian Government desires to renew the agreement for an additional period of 2
                    years under the authority contained in Title I, Article 2 of the basic
                    agreement.</p>
                <pb facs="0409" n="397" xml:id="pg397"/>
                <p>This is a routine inquiry, under the Department’s policy of making adequate
                    preparation in advance for renewal of missions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
